{
  "title": "Bridge get_oracle_text misses ordinary card-name lookups",
  "description": "In `~/.mage-bench/logs/game_20260320_102217/`, G54m Proud \
asked the bridge for oracle text by card name and got \
`Card not found in database` for ordinary non-token cards that were already \
in the live game state.\n\
\n\
Evidence:\n\
- `~/.mage-bench/logs/game_20260320_102217/G54m Proud_pilot.log:373-379` shows \
repeated `get_oracle_text` calls by name during turn 8. One call is malformed \
(`card_name` plus `card_names`), but the next call is a valid single-name \
lookup: `{\"card_name\":\"Locthwain \
Gargoyle\",\"card_names\":[],\"object_id\":\"\",\"object_ids\":[]}`.\n\
- `~/.mage-bench/logs/game_20260320_102217/G54m Proud_llm.jsonl:187` records \
the bridge response to that valid lookup: `{\"success\":false,\"error\":\"Card \
not found in database: Locthwain Gargoyle\"}`.\n\
- The failure is specific to name lookup, not oracle extraction in general. \
Later in the same game, `~/.mage-bench/logs/game_20260320_102217/G54m \
Proud_llm.jsonl:293-294` successfully resolves the same board via object IDs: \
`object_id=\"p11\"` returns Locthwain Gargoyle and `object_id=\"p29\"` returns \
Golem Artisan.\n\
\n\
Source:\n\
- \
`Mage.Client.Bridge/src/main/java/mage/client/bridge/BridgeOracleTextService.java:75-120` \
routes `card_name` / `card_names` requests through \
`CardRepository.instance.findCard(...)` and emits `Card not found in database: \
...` on miss.\n\
- \
`Mage.Client.Bridge/src/main/java/mage/client/bridge/BridgeClient.java:82-85` \
explicitly skips the bulk `CardScanner.scan()` warmup in bridge mode and \
relies on lazy name loads instead.\n\
- The likely failure point is the lazy name-load path in \
`Mage/src/main/java/mage/cards/repository/CardRepository.java:446-464` \
(invoked from `CardRepository.java:509-512`). Inference from the logs: the \
live bridge runtime is not populating `CardRepository` reliably enough for \
ordinary `get_oracle_text(card_name=...)` calls, even though live `CardView` \
lookups by object ID still work.\n\
\n\
Impact:\n\
- Models waste turns and context retrying a broken info tool.\n\
- Name-based oracle lookups are unreliable even for normal cards already \
visible on the battlefield, which pushes models toward object-ID workarounds \
or repeated failed calls.\n\
\n\
Suggested fix:\n\
- Make bridge startup guarantee that `CardRepository.findCard(name)` works for \
normal cards in bridge mode, or add a bridge-side fallback when the repository \
misses.\n\
- Add a bridge test that starts with bulk scanning disabled and verifies \
`get_oracle_text(card_name=\"Locthwain Gargoyle\")` succeeds.\n\
\n\
Checked `git log --oneline --since=\"2026-03-20\" origin/master`; there is no \
obvious post-game fix for bridge oracle-name lookup.",
